│ environmental stimuli (Wooldridge & Jennings, 1995), whereas modern language │
│ model approaches rely on dynamic, generative reasoning traces and linguistic │
│ prompts (Wei et al., 2022; Yao et al., 2023a). Moreover, while frameworks    │
│ like ReAct manage reasoning and acting within a single model loop (Yao et    │
│ al., 2023a), AutoGen and CAMEL shift the paradigm toward distributed         │
│ multi-agent conversations and cooperative role-playing (Wu et al., 2023; Li  │
│ et al., 2023). These differences stem from whether a task is assumed to be   │
│ solvable via linear introspection or enhanced through interactive agent      │
│ specialization.                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│ Critical gaps remain within the current literature. A prominent              │
│ vulnerability is the lack of verifiable execution models, which leads        │
│ directly to planning breakdowns and cascading errors (Valmeekam et al.,      │
