│ architectures and multi-agent frameworks are widely proposed, the corpus     │
│ lacks explicit empirical scale bounds regarding communication overhead,      │
│ latency, and performance degradation in large-scale deployments. As a        │
│ plausible implication not explicitly stated in the texts, building           │
│ production-grade agents will likely require combining formal verification    │
│ layers with dynamic memory updates to ensure safety during unconstrained     │
│ execution.                                                                   │
│                                                                              │
│ Conclusion                                                                   │
│                                                                              │
│ Building AI agents that can reason and act requires a synthesis of           │
│ foundational component decomposition, prompt-based reasoning mechanisms,     │
│ multi-agent collaboration protocols, and external knowledge grounding. The   │
│ main approaches transition from early reactive stimulus-response models      │
